    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91155" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτερῠγ-ίζω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1466
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτέρυξ</span>):—<i>flutter
				with the wings</i>, like young birds trying to
			fly, ib.<i><span class="en">
				795
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				1466
			</span></i>; <i>flap the wings</i>, like a cock crowing,
			metaph. of a man, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				575
			</span></i>; of sea-birds, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Sign.</u>
				28
			</span></i>:—in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				522
			</span></i> the word alludes to the play <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄρνιθες</span> by Magnes.</div>
